 COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT:\r\r No one indicated a desire to speak.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of meeting minutes from June 24, and August 12, 2009. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2009-1191, adopting Human Resource Guidelines and rescinding Resolution No. 2002-770. \r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2009-262, amending Appendix K of Title 15 of the Municipal Code Section 15.104.610 adopting Code amendments and a comprehensive Onsite Waste Water Treatment System Operating permit program. \r\r Recommendation to accept completion for the Las Virgenes Corridor Signal Interconnect Specification No. 07-08-16 by TDS Engineering, and to direct the City Clerk to file notice of completion. \r\r Authorization to approve change order no. two in the amount of $92,850 utilizing existing funding for Vandergeest Landscape to perform required and proposed extra work as part of Specification No. 07-08-05 landscape maintenance of the common areas outside individual homeowner associations and commercial properties within Landscape Maintenance Districts 24, 27 & 32 within the City of Calabasas. \r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to approve Consent Items 1, 4, and 5. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r Robin Parker, Administrative Services Director, presented background information on Item #2.\r\r Councilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve Consent Item #2. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Mayor pro Tem Groveman was not present.\r\r Shelly Palmer, Calabasas, Matt Young, Calabasas, Jody Thomas, Calabasas, Gail Newman, Calabasas, Toby Keeler, Topanga, Babette Gibbs, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to the proposed ordinance in Item #3.\r\r Sparky Cohen, Building Official, provided background information on Item #3.\r\rFollowing discussion, Mayor pro Tem Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve Consent Item #3 with further direction. MOTION CARRIED 4/1. Councilmember Bozajian voted NO.\r\rNEW BUSINESS \r\r Discussion of Resolution No. 2009-1204, approving a fee schedule for Onsite Waste Water Treatment System (OWTS) Operating permit program. \r\r Sparky Cohen, Building Official, presented a staff report.\r \rThe Council concurred to continue the item to a future meeting.\r\r Feasibility of sewer expansion in Old Topanga. \r\rAnita Davidoo, Associate Engineer, presented the staff report.\r\rJody Thomas, Calabasas, Toby Keeler, Calabasas, Babette Gibbs, Calabasas, Russ Sutherland, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to proposed sewer expansion in Old Topanga. Jan Dubin, Calabasas, spoke in support of being connected to the sewer system but spoke regarding the high cost of connection.\r \rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Groveman to continue the item to the meeting of September 9, 2009. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2009-1205, amending the Parks and Recreation Master Plan by incorporating the following:�the City of Calabasas shall not expand upon the current footprint or facilities of Gates Canyon Park. \r\rJeff Rubin, Community Services Director, presented the staff report.\r\rCarol Elliott, Mountain View Estates, expressed concern that the City could potentially develop the open space property under Ordinance No. 2005-225.\r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to adopt Resolution No. 2009-1205, amending the Parks and Recreation Master Plan. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2009-1206, affirming the City�s intent to the residents of Mountain View Estates regarding preservation of their designated open space. \r\rCouncilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to adopt Resolution No. 2009-1206 with the addition of a �whereas� clause. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of August 4, 2009 to August 12, 2009. \r\r There was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r There were no task force reports.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r The City Council requested future agenda items on the update on the ban on plastic bans and an ordinance regarding requiring encroachment permits for construction on areas with narrow streets.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015ADJOURN\r \r The City Council adjourned at 9:45 p.m. to the next regularly scheduled meeting on Wednesday, September 9, 2009 at 7:00 p.m.\r\r\r\r\r\r\r__________________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC, City Clerk\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00143\u0015\r08/26/09\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\